show version
    show version

##) SYNOPSIS:

    ```sh nuts version [<-options>]```
    ```sh nuts --version```
    ```sh nuts -version```
    ```sh nuts -v```
        Although `nuts -v` seems as a shortcut for `nuts version`, the reality is that they behave differently.
        `nuts version` command loads workspace and shows api/runtime versions (the actual workspace version).
        `nuts -v|-version|--version` commands shows boot version only and does not load any workspace.

##) OPTIONS:

    ```sh -a | --all```
        include all versions (api, runtime, ##:_:Java™## and operating system)

    ```sh --add <key>=<value> ```
        include key=value pair in the result

```!include classpath:/net/thevpc/nuts/runtime/includes/standard-command.ntf```

##) EXAMPLES

    ```sh nuts version -a```
        show all versions

    ```sh nuts -v```
        show version

    ```sh nuts -Zy -w test version --table ```
        show version in tabular format
